  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "Z.TEST and ZTEST check sample size even with sigma supplied and evaluate NORMSDIST((x - mean) * sqrt(n) / sigma)",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20326 and 20527, Z.TEST(array, x, [sigma]) requires the _xlfn. prefix in OOXML (bare @Z.TEST returns #NAME?) while compatibility ZTEST takes no prefix. Both validate sample length even when sigma is provided (0 values -> #N/A, 1 value -> #DIV/0!), use sample STDEV.S when sigma is omitted, and compute NORMSDIST((x - mean) * sqrt(n) / sigma); grouping as (x - mean) / (sigma / sqrt(n)) or 1 - NORMSDIST((mean - x)/se) differs by 1 ULP. Matches 2,857/2,857 Z.TEST and 2,864/2,864 ZTEST full-bank rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20326 Value2 probes (confidence_test_family.rs lines 97-117), Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (rows 243-244), and full-bank witness sets (2,857/2,857 Z.TEST and 2,864/2,864 ZTEST).",
